    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a3c5eeab_1ad66a96",
        "filename": "bazel/external/vello/BUILD.bazel",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-19T18:12:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that this can be error-prone though with Rust the convention is for all Rust files under `src/` to be automatically referenced in the build (assuming they are also referenced via `mod` statements at module boundaries). vello_shaders and vello_encoding both follow the conventional crate structure and I expect everything that matches this glob to be valid Rust sources. I used bazel/externals/cxx/BUILD.bazel.skia as precedent.\n\nThe exception is for `cargo_build_script` where I enumerated the rust build.rs file and the various rust sources that it includes as explicit data dependencies, since that falls outside the category of a \"conventional crate structure\". Build scripts aren\u0027t crates after all. I still listed all the vello shader files as a glob as there are many of them, however they follow the project convention of \"`.wgsl` files under the top-level `shader/` directory\".",
      "parentUuid": "9921268f_1bfc7845",
      "range": {
